            <ArticleTitle>A rare cause of an acute abdomen in late pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>435-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is presented where spontaneous rupture of a uterine arteriovenous malformation into the peritoneal cavity presented as an acute abdomen with fetal distress in late pregnancy. This is thought to be the first reported case of its type.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
